MUST_FIX 1 — P100, both halves

1a  MIS-CITATION. profile.yaml knowledge_partition.always_on[10] (expertise/transfer) cited
    P100 — reading-diagnostic measure selection — which that paragraph never restates, and
    which was cited nowhere else in the profile. Citation dropped. The remaining ten (P005,
    P009, P018, P039, P104, P108, P117, P122, P128, P131) already ground every claim in the
    paragraph, so nothing became unsupported. The expertise-development-and-transfer SKILL
    KEEPS P100 — it routes on it (trigger 4) and restates it advisorily at Procedure step 2 —
    so the principle keeps a home. .build/authoring/gen.py gained an ALWAYS_ON_EXCLUDE set so
    a regeneration cannot silently re-add the false link.

1b  BARE ACT-ON-A-LEARNER IMPERATIVE IN THE ALWAYS-ON LAYER. The invariant compiler strips
    applies_when, so P100 reached the always-loaded layer as the unconditional "Collect
    real-word reading, spelling ability and word attack skills as the diagnostic measures" —
    the only one of the 54 invariants phrased as an instruction to act on an individual, and
    in tension with forbidden_behaviours[1] (diagnosing a learner), when_not_to_use[1] and the
    router's diagnosis exclusion. The statement now survives stripping on its own:

      "When advising on assessment for a persistent reading difficulty, recommend real-word
       reading, spelling ability and word attack skills as the diagnostic measures to collect,
       since they are the greatest predictors of reading comprehension."

    Grounding: the condition is P100's own applies_when[1] plus C04895's recorded condition
    ("when evaluating or supporting reading difficulty"); the "greatest predictors of reading
    comprehension" clause is verbatim from C03615. The advisory verb matches the skill body's
    existing wording. Nothing strengthened, nothing invented.

