Gate:    reports/review-loop/learning-science-advisor.verify1.md (MUST_FIX_COUNT: 3)
Result:  validate = VALIDATION PASSED, 0 FAIL, 1 WARN (pre-existing quote-scan).

All three must-fix findings were of one class — a boundary rule citing principle codes whose
`statement` in principles/principles.yaml does not state it. Fixes are provenance-only:
no boundary was weakened, no new claim was introduced, and every remaining P### resolves to
a statement that carries the clause it is attached to.

MF1 — forbidden_behaviours[0]  (P010, P077) → (authored scope boundary)
      P010 is mechanism-first translation into a local implementation; P077 is not treating
      one's own learning history as proof. Neither is about WHO performs teaching, delivery,
      authoring, or marking. Boundary text unchanged, hedge complete.

MF2 — forbidden_behaviours[2]  (P128, P087) → (authored scope boundary)
      P128 governs WHAT to assess (plural competence dimensions, not one static score);
      P087 governs PACING to demonstrated readiness. Neither states an authority boundary on
      placement, grading, admission, promotion, or employment outcomes. Boundary text unchanged.

MF3 — handoff_rules[0]  (P010, P077) → (P010) on the supported clause + (authored scope boundary)
      Ownership of curriculum, materials, delivery, and marks is an authored authority
      allocation. P010 retained only on the clause it genuinely supports: the design reasoning
      is adapted through each principle's mechanism to the local learners, format, and
      institution. P077 dropped (silent on ownership).

ADVISORY (same defect class, fixed in the same pass as verify1 recommends)
      handoff_rules[1]  (P134, P128) → (authored scope boundary) + (P134) on the clause P134
      states: group categories ground bounded population inference, not individual capacity
      judgments. P128 grounds neither "belongs to a qualified specialist" nor "to the
      responsible body".

BODY-SIZE SIDE EFFECT (phase8 check 14, hard FAIL > 1000 words)
      The 1.2.0 body stood at exactly 1000 words. The honest tags plus the two retained
      grounding clauses (longer than the codes they replace) took it to 1011 → FAIL.
      Recovered to 998 by trimming WORDING ONLY — never a citation, hedge, or boundary clause:
      role (source-type description; the `sources` pointer and the "invariants are advisory
      criteria, not authority to act" disambiguation kept verbatim), when_to_use[1],
      inputs.required 1–5 (phrasing only; ask-for-missing-context, Glob/Grep, root-relative
      resolution, and never-cite-a-code-from-memory all keep full operative content),
      outputs.primary_format, advise mode output.

UNCHANGED: all 150 principles, 15 skills, 2 references, tests, the 54-line invariant layer,
the advice-only role, and every other subagent package.
